<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turgut Reis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1485–<a href="/years/1565">1565</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Dragut</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Turgut Reis, known in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> as Dragut, was an Ottoman corsair and admiral. A lieutenant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayreddin-barbarossa">Hayreddin Barbarossa</a>, he raided the coasts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, helped take Tripoli from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> in 1551 and became its governor, and defeated a Spanish fleet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djerba">Djerba</a> in 1560. He was killed during the Great Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a> in 1565.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/turgut-reis.jpg" alt="Turgut Reis" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Josep Renalias · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Istanbul_-_Est%C3%A0tua_de_Turgut_Reis_sota_el_Palau_de_Topkapi_retouched.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
